mem:constraint-01m5y26y2g6hjydmb652z0sb3w a mem:Constraint ;
    mem:content "bus_wake never marks mail read: it reads through Bus.deliver (passing over only non-mail) and moves only an in-memory woken mark per address and join (the unread span, first to newest). Marks move in one step while the call is still the session's current wait, and are put back if the result is not returned. It is annotated closed-world and non-destructive but not read-only, since it moves that mark." ;
    mem:tag "annotations" ;
    mem:tag "claude" ;
    mem:tag "cursors" ;
    mem:tag "wake" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:severity "must" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/Bus.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/mcp.ts" ;
    mem:branch "claude-host-wake" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T06:54:21.776907Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:decision-01m5y26y0mphzhke0krefx8rhb a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "Claude Code sessions are woken by the agent-bus plugin (plugin/, a single manifest): an asyncRewake hook on SessionStart, Stop and StopFailure runs ~/.local/bin/agent-bus claude-wake, which waits in bus_wake until an address the session holds as claude, joined from this machine, has unread mail other than what it was last woken for, then prints a fixed nudge to call bus_read and exits 2. bus_join returns hooked: true once serve has seen the session's hook (held in serve's memory). A session without the plugin isn't woken; it reads with bus_read or bus_wait. Plugin monitors were rejected: they don't start in stream-json mode, how the desktop app runs Claude Code." ;
    mem:tag "claude" ;
    mem:tag "hooks" ;
    mem:tag "plugin" ;
    mem:tag "wake" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef ".claude-plugin/plugin.json" ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/frames/claude-wake.md" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/Bus.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/claude.ts" ;
    mem:branch "claude-host-wake" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T06:54:21.716683Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:updatedAt "2026-10-27T23:36:03.921722+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "The host re-arms the wake at session start and every turn end, so the model starts nothing, in the desktop app (stream-json mode) and the terminal alike." ;
    mem:alternatives "a plugin monitor running a streaming watch (never starts in stream-json mode; desktop sessions run that way),serve posting into the session inbox socket (held for sessions that bypass permissions; the desktop drops held messages after five minutes),channels (terminal only)" .

mem:fact-01m5y26y48w2rk3e0yh14fszrs a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "Claude Code 2.1.310: plugin monitors never start in stream-json mode (how the desktop app runs Claude Code), though the plugin loads; in an interactive terminal they start once the folder is trusted, run for the whole session with no deadline, and keep the session id from before /clear. asyncRewake hooks (Stop or SessionStart, from settings or a plugin) wake an idle stream-json session on exit 2, a SessionStart one with no prompt sent; their timeout is enforced (killed at it, no wake) and 2592000 s is accepted." ;
    mem:tag "claude" ;
    mem:tag "hooks" ;
    mem:tag "monitors" ;
    mem:tag "trap" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/frames/claude-wake.md" ;
    mem:branch "claude-host-wake" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T06:54:21.832877Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:fact-01m5y26y5y9r72px418615x6tq a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "Effect 4.0.6 McpServer returns a declared tool failure that is an Error with a message as plain text (the message alone), not its encoded JSON, so a client can't tell a LedgerError from a NotOwner by type. The Claude wake hook therefore checks the session itself and retries every failed bus_wake call for up to ten minutes." ;
    mem:tag "effect" ;
    mem:tag "errors" ;
    mem:tag "mcp" ;
    mem:tag "trap" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/claude.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/client.ts" ;
    mem:branch "claude-host-wake" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T06:54:21.886327Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:constraint-01m5x9h52psxmgtkmg6pxw27q8 a mem:Constraint ;
    mem:content "A process started from a session's shell inherits that session's runtime id (codex exec from Claude inherits CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID), so the CLI acts as the parent when it defaults --runtime to the address's runtime. Give delegates that need an inbox their own address." ;
    mem:tag "delegates" ;
    mem:tag "identity" ;
    mem:tag "ownership" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:severity "should" ;
    mem:artifactRef "README.md" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-26T23:43:02.230648Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:constraint-01m5xn3cfyazcft2fzpm61vfvp a mem:Constraint ;
    mem:content "thread/queue/add does not deduplicate on clientUserMessageId: adding twice queues two items, and the desktop runs both. List the thread's queue before adding. The thread/queue/* methods are experimental (initialize with experimentalApi); use the desktop's bundled CLI so they match the app that runs the items." ;
    mem:tag "app-server" ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "queue" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:severity "must" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/codex.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T03:05:13.982763Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:constraint-01m5xpmd26mdncn7hmmkp0b53j a mem:Constraint ;
    mem:content "Never edit, branch or check out anything but a deployed main in the primary agent-bus checkout: the LaunchAgent's serve runs src/bin.ts from it, and every Claude session's wake hook runs it through the installer's link ~/.local/bin/agent-bus. A half-edited tree breaks serve at its next restart and the hooks at their next run. Develop in a worktree; the primary checkout changes only by a fast-forward merge at deploy." ;
    mem:tag "hooks" ;
    mem:tag "operations" ;
    mem:tag "serve" ;
    mem:tag "worktree" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:severity "must" ;
    mem:artifactRef "README.md" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/bin.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T03:32:00.198214Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:updatedAt "2026-10-27T23:36:03.963355+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Found 2026-10-27 when a simplification edit in the primary checkout made the running wait fail to import; the hook and a serve restart would have failed the same way." .

mem:constraint-01m5xxta54dma2s3jwfcbhk54n a mem:Constraint ;
    mem:content "serve loads a Codex thread only to run its own queued nudge, and only through the machine's daemon: after posting under the address's lock, it reads the thread's rollout and, if the thread is eligible, borrows it (thread/resume with excludeTurns and config thread_unload_delay_secs 5, then thread/unsubscribe, then disconnect). It starts or steers no turn and waits for none; the writer lock refuses the borrow while another process holds the thread, and that process runs the nudge. Eligible means: approval never, Default collaboration mode, permissions a resume keeps (full access, read-only, or a built-in profile whose saved form denies nothing), and no client-registered dynamic tools. Anything unreadable is ineligible." ;
    mem:tag "app-server" ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "daemon" ;
    mem:tag "guard" ;
    mem:tag "queue" ;
    mem:tag "wake" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:severity "must" ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/frames/load-on-mail.md" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/codex.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/rollout.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T05:37:33.860507Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:updatedAt "2026-10-28T04:43:17.635129+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "A thread has one writer. Resuming a desktop-app thread once the app released it made the daemon its writer and locked the owner's window ('open in another app'). A queued item runs in whichever app-server has the thread loaded, so adding one needs no knowledge of where the thread lives." ;
    mem:alternatives "classifying each join's host (codexHost) and resuming only daemon threads (a wait at every join; stale once the thread moves),retrying a refused resume with back-off (contends with the owner's app)" .

mem:constraint-01m5xxtabswcyy08b31skk6s4z a mem:Constraint ;
    mem:content "Every bus MCP tool must be annotated openWorldHint false and, except bus_join, destructiveHint false; pure lookups also readOnlyHint true. bus_join stays destructive because a takeover replaces another session's hold. Effect's ai Tool defaults to destructive and open-world, and Codex then asks approval for each call outside full access, or refuses it under approval policy never, so a nudged thread can't read or answer its mail." ;
    mem:tag "annotations" ;
    mem:tag "approval" ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "mcp" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:severity "must" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/mcp.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "test/mcp-official.test.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T05:37:34.073037Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:updatedAt "2026-10-27T05:37:46.116492Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Codex's requires_mcp_tool_approval requires approval when destructiveHint is true, or when a tool isn't read-only and destructiveHint or openWorldHint is unset or true; only policy never with full disk write access, or a server approval mode of approve, skips that. Found live when a read-only-sandbox thread ran its nudge and bus_read was refused; the Stop hook masked it by delivering at turn end." .

mem:constraint-01m5zvh3rypm1qrxpmr95bc8y8 a mem:Constraint ;
    mem:content "src/bin.ts's shebang must keep bun's --no-env-file (#!/usr/bin/env -S bun --no-env-file): the Claude wake hook runs in the session's project directory, and bun otherwise loads that project's .env, which can set AGENT_BUS_PORT or other variables and point the hook at the wrong bus." ;
    mem:tag "bun" ;
    mem:tag "claude" ;
    mem:tag "env" ;
    mem:tag "hooks" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:severity "must" ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/frames/finish-swap.md" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/bin.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T23:36:04.126583+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:decision-01m5x1zt1sy4dfmyp66p7ah4ep a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "Each machine runs one agent-bus serve that owns the store for that machine's sessions; sessions and the CLI reach it over MCP (streamable HTTP on loopback), and it also runs the Codex deliverer." ;
    mem:tag "architecture" ;
    mem:tag "mcp" ;
    mem:tag "serve" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/Bus.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/serve.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-26T21:31:13.849993Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "One process gives one cursor writer per address, one per-address lock (Bus.deliver) shared by reads and deliveries, and one ledger change stream; only serve holds the Fluree token." ;
    mem:alternatives "a stdio MCP server per session (raced on cursors and needed the token in every session),Fluree's native MCP endpoint for agents,a separate deliver-codex process" .

mem:decision-01m5x1zt9exbx6s973sqkt00kh a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "Codex desktop Local threads stay in the desktop app's own app-server. The bus wakes them, idle or busy, with a nudge in their own queue (see the queue-wake decision)." ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "desktop" ;
    mem:tag "hooks" ;
    mem:tag "wake" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/connections.md" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/codex.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-26T21:31:14.094317Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:updatedAt "2026-10-27T06:31:43.296056Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Moving desktop threads onto the daemon loses desktop features the owner needs: SSH projects lose browser and computer use, automations and the artifact viewer, and probably Handoff and the thread tools; the CODEX_APP_SERVER_WS_URL override skips the app's provisioning too." ;
    mem:alternatives "a desktop SSH project to the same machine,launching the app with CODEX_APP_SERVER_WS_URL,deep links (they only prefill the composer)" .

mem:decision-01m5x9h50yh252vteyr31k9jtk a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "Each bus address is owned by one session, identified by (runtime, the runtime's own id: CODEX_THREAD_ID or CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID), passed as an explicit session argument on every call and recorded in the presence entry. Only the owner reads, waits, leaves or sends from it; takeover must name the holder's join id." ;
    mem:tag "addresses" ;
    mem:tag "identity" ;
    mem:tag "ownership" ;
    mem:tag "takeover" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/frames/address-ownership.md" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/Bus.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/client.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-26T23:43:02.174817Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Two sessions on one address were competing consumers: a reply went to the wrong session. Runtime ids survive compaction and reach background waits and hooks without extra storage." ;
    mem:alternatives "lease token issued at join (must survive compaction and be handed to waits and hooks),identity in an HTTP header (connection headers stay fixed across /clear; one Codex daemon serves many threads),idle-based automatic takeover (inactivity cannot prove a session ended)" .

mem:decision-01m5xn3ccvw8spz95s87csea3r a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "A Codex thread is woken by a nudge in its own queue: serve starts a short-lived app-server of its own on stdio (the desktop's bundled CLI, serve --codex), lists the thread's queue (thread/queue/list, every page) and adds one fixed nudge (thread/queue/add) only when none of ours waits for that address. The nudge carries no text from other sessions and marks nothing read; the thread's own bus_read moves its cursor." ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "delivery" ;
    mem:tag "desktop" ;
    mem:tag "queue" ;
    mem:tag "wake" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/frames/queue-wake.md" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/codex.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T03:05:13.883838Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:updatedAt "2026-10-27T05:37:33.994907Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "The desktop app runs a queued item as a turn within seconds in an idle open thread and stays the thread's only writer. Listing before adding keeps at most one nudge waiting, which bounds empty turns to one per read, survives serve restarts and reconciles adds whose outcome is unknown." ;
    mem:alternatives "the desktop coordination socket (spike, never run past Gate 0),a heartbeat automation in the thread (crude fallback only),the daemon taking the thread (second writer locks the owner out),the codex queue CLI with an in-memory mark (reads before a nudge runs stack empty turns; timed-out adds force duplicate or missed wake),thread/queue/start (could run the item in an app-server that is not the thread's owner)" .

mem:decision-01m5xxta7vr0wb7b7640a0wqyv a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "Every Codex thread is woken by a content-free nudge in its own queue that tells it to call bus_read; a thread loaded nowhere is then borrowed by the daemon so the nudge runs, if it is eligible. serve sends no messages as turns, steers no busy turn and marks nothing read; only the owner's read (bus_read or bus_wait) marks its mail read. Unread mail is reconciled 5, 15 and 60 minutes after the attempt that covered it, then hourly, re-posting a nudge that has gone. With nothing for the subscriber, serve moves its cursor past entries that aren't its mail, as that read would." ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "delivery" ;
    mem:tag "queue" ;
    mem:tag "wake" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/architecture/delivery.md" ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/frames/load-on-mail.md" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/codex.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T05:37:33.947759Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:updatedAt "2026-10-28T04:43:17.673600+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Agents are woken, never polled. The daemon runs a queued item for a thread it has loaded, with or without a client attached, within seconds when idle and after the current turn when busy, and keeps it for a thread nothing has loaded until one resumes it. So the daemon route's resume, turn/start, host classification and holds bought only steering and headless resume, at the cost of a second path that writes to threads and most of the delivery code. The empty-batch skip stays because Fluree's read from a cursor queries every commit up to the head, so a peer with no mail would otherwise re-read a growing range on every change." ;
    mem:alternatives "keeping the daemon route for steering and closed TUI threads (a second writer path that nothing relied on),marking mail read when the nudge is queued (a lost nudge then loses the mail),dropping the empty-batch skip (the cost grows with the ledger)" .

mem:decision-01m5y0xfhgx4cre4rg53xnyzwh a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "Messages live in a Fluree ledger (one message per insert commit; a cursor is the last commit t read), behind the Ledger service. It is the only production store: serve won't start without a fluree entry in config.json. The unit tests use a JSONL ledger (test/jsonl-ledger.ts)." ;
    mem:tag "fluree" ;
    mem:tag "ledger" ;
    mem:tag "store" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/Fluree.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/bin.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "test/jsonl-ledger.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T06:31:43.408992Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "The ledger is queryable (SPARQL SELECT and full-text through bus_query and bus_history), readable as of any t, and shared by every machine through one transaction server. A second production store doubled what had to stay correct, for a fallback nothing used once every machine had Fluree." ;
    mem:alternatives "JSONL as a fallback production store (unused once every machine had Fluree),SQLite" .

mem:decision-01m5y0xfm8zx0cxdqqxm1nrm3p a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "Every entry records its origin: the machine, the session's joined directory, and that directory's Git repo and branch as optional metadata (bus:repo, bus:branch) for queries. Each git call gets 2 seconds under the address's lock; a field it misses is left out. No commit-window view is built." ;
    mem:tag "git" ;
    mem:tag "metadata" ;
    mem:tag "origin" ;
    mem:tag "query" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/Bus.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/domain.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T06:31:43.496623Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "A branch is a cheap proxy for the workstream and task behind a message, and can't be recovered once its worktree or branch is gone; it is recorded per entry, not per join, because a session can switch branches. The owner plans richer ledger properties so history can be queried by meaning, and repo and branch are the first of them." ;
    mem:alternatives "recording repo and branch once at join (misses branch switches),dropping them (the workstream context can't be reconstructed),a Git SHA per message (a git call per send that says nothing for uncommitted work)" .

mem:decision-01m5y0xfnyv3fhekaj29gcg196 a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "The Codex Stop hook is retired, and so is the codex-stop-hook command that covered the transition: a nudged turn reads the mail itself with bus_read. Codex builds a thread's hooks when it loads the thread, so removing a hook takes effect only for threads loaded after every app-server (the desktop app's and the daemon) has restarted; check start times with ps -o lstart before removing anything a loaded thread could still call." ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "hooks" ;
    mem:tag "retired" ;
    mem:tag "wake" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/frames/simplification-pass.md" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/bin.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T06:31:43.550044Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:updatedAt "2026-10-27T23:36:04.033848+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "With approval-free reads, the nudge alone delivers to idle, busy, clientless and unloaded threads. The hook's remaining effects were inline delivery at a busy turn's end, the empty turn after it, and hiding a failed read. Codex keeps a loaded thread's hooks until its app-server restarts, so deleting the command at once would record a failure at every turn end of those threads." ;
    mem:alternatives "deleting the command at once (recorded failures until each app-server restarts),two deploys with the no-op first (guards only against one recorded failure),keeping the hook (message text in the turn and an extra empty turn)" .

mem:decision-01m5zvh3qar2276yby9g3xqbmd a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "The Claude Code plugin's hook runs the checkout through the link ~/.local/bin/agent-bus -> src/bin.ts, not through ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}: claude plugin install from a local-directory marketplace copies the plugin into ~/.claude/plugins/cache/<marketplace>/<plugin>/<sha>, so a path inside the plugin root is a stale copy. The installer makes the link and checks it runs with a launchd-style PATH from /." ;
    mem:tag "claude" ;
    mem:tag "deploy" ;
    mem:tag "hooks" ;
    mem:tag "plugin" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/frames/finish-swap.md" ;
    mem:artifactRef "plugin/.claude-plugin/plugin.json" ;
    mem:artifactRef "scripts/install-launch-agents.sh" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T23:36:04.074554+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "One stable manifest, and the hook always runs the deployed checkout without a plugin update per release" ;
    mem:alternatives "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/src/bin.ts (a cached copy, stale after each deploy); per-machine path configuration" .

mem:fact-01m5x1ztcfrgxg1r3zcbxt5s0f a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "The bus's Fluree token has no subject and is sent only to the data and admin APIs; the event stream stays open. In Fluree 4.2.4 a token with a subject is held to identity policies, which deny writes on a ledger without policies, and events auth refuses subject-less tokens. With CORS off, a cross-origin text/plain POST still writes, so auth is what protects the loopback server." ;
    mem:tag "auth" ;
    mem:tag "fluree" ;
    mem:tag "security" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "scripts/install-launch-agents.sh" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/Fluree.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-26T21:31:14.191984Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Each of these was found by a failing write or test during setup." .

mem:fact-01m5x1zte4rznzfcj9npy234jz a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "HttpRouter.serve forks its layer memo map, so a service built inside it is a separate instance from one built outside. Provide Bus (and the Ledger) around Serve.layer, never inside the router, or the MCP tools and the Codex deliverer get separate cursors and locks." ;
    mem:tag "effect" ;
    mem:tag "layers" ;
    mem:tag "serve" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/serve.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-26T21:31:14.244634Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Found in Effect 4.0.6's source while wiring serve; nothing fails visibly, deliveries just stop being serialized with reads." .

mem:fact-01m5x1ztfs8vfda4m06w25nvj8 a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "codex app-server daemon stop and restart act only on a daemon the managed lifecycle started (daemon start); they leave one an SSH-project proxy or the CLI auto-started. A managed daemon runs an update loop by default, for a stable standalone release only, and restarts on a new version (Codex 0.164, read in code). On the bus host a desktop SSH project from another machine restarts a stopped daemon within about 5 s, unmanaged, from the desktop's bundled CLI (its SSH connection starts it; codex app-server proxy itself only connects). A running daemon keeps the login it started with: after a Codex login change its turns run as the old user (seen as 'out of credits') until it restarts. To replace an unmanaged one, kill -TERM it by PID; restarting drops its loaded threads." ;
    mem:tag "app-server" ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "daemon" ;
    mem:tag "operations" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/platforms/codex.md" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-26T21:31:14.297018Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:updatedAt "2026-10-28T04:43:17.710501+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "The daemon inherits its starter's open-file limit (macOS default 256), and each loaded thread costs about 33 descriptors, so a few threads exhaust it." .

mem:fact-01m5xn3chn8n8q5wktct3xxn4s a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "A Codex thread has no rollout until its first turn, so thread/queue/add for a just-started thread fails with 'no rollout found'; that error can be temporary and is retried. Separately, codex exec reads stdin when it is not a terminal and waits on it, even with a prompt argument: run it with < /dev/null in scripts." ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "exec" ;
    mem:tag "queue" ;
    mem:tag "rollout" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/frames/queue-wake.md" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T03:05:14.037431Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:fact-01m5xnf9zqad6yt71b5exbs2dc a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "The Codex app-server daemon runs a queued item (thread/queue/add from another process) as a turn for any thread it has loaded, with or without a client attached, within seconds when idle; an item added mid-turn runs as its own turn after the current one. A thread nothing has loaded keeps the item until an app-server resumes it, which runs it at once. A spawned subagent's queue refuses the add ('direct app-server input is not allowed for unloaded spawned sub-agents'). Verified on Codex 0.164." ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "daemon" ;
    mem:tag "queue" ;
    mem:tag "wake" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/frames/queue-wake.md" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T03:11:44.631668Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:updatedAt "2026-10-27T05:37:34.030825Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:fact-01m5xp8sc3dxn0nzd394qprgrr a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "Effect 4.0.6 McpServer as official tooling sees it: any Origin is refused (403) unless in allowedOrigins, so the MCP conformance dns-rebinding check fails on a localhost Origin by design; an MCP-Protocol-Version header differing from the negotiated version gets 400 (-32020), though the spec requires 400 only for invalid or unsupported versions, failing conformance server-sse-multiple-streams; stateful versions always advertise completions, logging and tools.listChanged; tools carry default annotations (destructiveHint true, readOnlyHint false) unless set. Most conformance server scenarios need the reference server's fixture tools." ;
    mem:tag "conformance" ;
    mem:tag "effect" ;
    mem:tag "mcp" ;
    mem:tag "spec" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/mcp.ts" ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/serve.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T03:25:39.587953Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:fact-01m5y0xfrbrcwbym2ws681paww a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "Codex builds a thread's hooks once, when it loads the thread (Hooks::new at session construction), and never reloads them: editing hooks.json reaches a thread only after its app-server restarts. A Stop hook that exits 1 is recorded as a failure and never blocks a turn; only exit 2 with stderr, or decision block, continues the turn. Codex ignores a broken pipe on the hook's stdin. Read in openai/codex 0.164 source." ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "hooks" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "src/bin.ts" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T06:31:43.627731Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:fact-01m60d3nbs2fz6yv2hyvwgf417 a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "Codex runs no queued input for a thread whose status is Interrupted, and a resume restores that status, so a borrow loads such a thread and runs nothing (0.164, ext/queue/src/service.rs; seen live). A turn is interrupted by the user's Stop, or by a codex exec run exiting mid-turn: codex exec resume takes a nudge queued during its turn right after that turn, then exits and cuts it off. The queued nudge waits until new input starts a turn." ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "exec" ;
    mem:tag "limit" ;
    mem:tag "queue" ;
    mem:tag "wake" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/architecture/delivery.md" ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/platforms/codex.md" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-28T04:43:17.753257+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

mem:fact-01m5xp8mhr201tna2derhkerve a mem:Fact ;
    mem:content "The official MCP SDK Client (@modelcontextprotocol/sdk 1.x) validates a tool's structuredContent only when that client's own listTools() cached the tool's output schema, and never for a tool without one; a tool whose success schema is void lists no outputSchema and returns empty text. So wire tests call listTools first and also assert structuredContent equals the JSON in the first text block. SDK 1.x always offers its latest protocol (2025-11-25) at initialize with no option to choose; it cannot speak the stateless 2026-07-28." ;
    mem:tag "mcp" ;
    mem:tag "sdk" ;
    mem:tag "testing" ;
    mem:tag "trap" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "test/mcp-official.test.ts" ;
    mem:branch "test/official-mcp-client" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-10-27T03:25:34.648211Z"^^xsd:dateTime .
